Problem:
     When there are fewer than 10 entries in the topten list, and you
     reach the medusa level, it's possible for the game to dump core.

Detailed Description:
     in makelevel(), the code for making named statues calls
     mk_tt_object(), but never checks to make sure that the return value
     isn't NULL before using it.

     A side effect: mk_tt_object() calls tt_oname(), which reads the top
     ten list.  At about line 770, it checks if it didn't find an entry,
     and trys again.  Unfortunately, the top ten file was closed (at
     line 766), so the "try again" fails.  Furthermore, if it can't find
     any entry, it returns NULL, which causes the core dump, above.

Fix:
     Two parts.
     1) to make makelevel() handle a NULL object returned
        from mk_tt_object().  My fix causes fewer statues to appear if
	there aren't any matches (a logical solution).
     2) to make tt_oname() try again correctly, by re-opening the top
        ten file.  The fix moves the pickentry label and some
	initialization code before the file-open code.

     I tried these out, and they worked much better.

